65:Source-page frontmatter is the routing layer's input. The model is responsible for declaring `products:` and `ingredients:` against the **existing** wiki taxonomy, not inventing slugs from the paper's text. Before writing any source page, check `wiki/products/` and `wiki/ingredients/` to know what slugs exist. Declared slugs are selected from that vocabulary; new slugs are not invented mid-ingest.
67:Empty `products: []` on a food or personal-care paper is a defect. A paper that measures heavy metals in any food product, personal-care product, dietary supplement, cosmetic, or any matrix that maps to a consumer-product category must declare at least one slug in `products:`. The one exception: if the natural match is a category Karen has not yet locked (no Step 0 Lock, no scaffolded row pages), the source declares `products: []` AND sets `pending_category_lock: <category-name>` in frontmatter. The routing audit picks the source up after the lock lands. Without the flag, the routing-discipline lint (`tools/audit-routing-discipline.mjs`) flags the source as a Phase 1 defect.
69:Broad-scope tokens are preferred over invented row-level slugs when the paper does not resolve the row split. If a paper measures "infant formula" generally without specifying powdered vs RTF vs soy vs non-soy, declare `products: [infant-formula]`, not `products: [infant-formula-powder-non-soy]`. The routing audit's `broadProductScopes` vocabulary fans broad scopes out via `route_kind: broad_formula_context`. Overspecifying frontmatter is worse than under-specifying it.
71:When the model writes the source page, it does not auto-create destination pages. Sources referencing an ingredient slug that doesn't exist surface as a `routing_unresolved.csv` entry; the autonomy loop's `tools/autonomy/create-missing-pages.mjs` creates ingredient stubs at frequency >= 2. Sources referencing a product slug that doesn't exist also surface in `routing_unresolved.csv` but the autonomy loop does **not** create the product stub — product pages are HMTc governance units requiring Karen's Step 0 Lock plus a scaffold-script commit. See CLAUDE.md Part 10 and `docs/order-of-operations.md` for the workflow.
79:Before ingest into a new HMTc category begins, the session verifies four things: the category's Step 0 Lock document exists, the scaffold script has created the row pages in `wiki/products/`, `wiki/products/index.md` includes a section for the category, and the master rollup page exists. If any of these are missing, the ingest defers all sources touching the category by setting `pending_category_lock: <category-name>` in source frontmatter and leaving `products: []`. The routing layer picks the source up after the lock lands. The model does not invent row-level slugs for not-yet-locked categories; doing so produces governance drift. See `docs/order-of-operations.md` Phase 0.
83:For this build, ingest means compiling a source into the persistent wiki system. It does not mean "the file is searchable now." The work is split across actors: **model** writes prose (source pages, narrative wiki content where appropriate); **system** scripts handle routing and structured-evidence emission; **generators** rebuild product-page tables and other compiled views; **Karen** decides scope, names new pages, and approves limit-setting work.
85:A source is not counted as ingested until all applicable steps below are complete:
87:1. [Karen] preserve the raw source and verify provenance.
88:2. [model] create or update the canonical source page at `wiki/sources/<cite-key>.md`, filling in frontmatter accurately (especially `products`, `ingredients`, `matrices`, `metals`, `jurisdictions`).
90:4. [system, per CLAUDE.md Part 5b] route the source by rebuilding `data/evidence/product_source_routing_audit.csv`. The model does not write routing rows.
91:5. [model, on Karen's approval] create a stub page if the destination doesn't exist (a `routing_unresolved` ingredient or product). The model proposes; Karen approves; the model creates the stub with required frontmatter.
95:If automation cannot place evidence cleanly, do not silently drop the source. The routing audit emits `routing_unresolved.csv` and `routing_malformed.csv` when source frontmatter does not connect or is malformed; the structured-evidence reingest queue flags value-level extraction work. Missing placements stay visible and recoverable.
99:When Karen drops a file into `raw/` and says "ingest this", the model's deliverable is the source page plus a list of any new pages the routing layer flags as unresolved. Routing fan-out, ingredient `contamination_profile` updates, and product-page table regeneration are downstream system passes, not part of the ingest itself.
103:3. [model] Create the source page using the template in [[docs/page-templates]]. Frontmatter accuracy is load-bearing because it feeds the routing layer; fill `products`, `ingredients`, `matrices`, `metals`, `jurisdictions` at the level of specificity the source actually states.
