3:This document covers operational conventions: units, naming, links, cite-keys, evidence grading, index/log formats, and out-of-scope rules. Rule-grade summary lives in CLAUDE.md.
11:**HMT&C analyte vocabulary:** The current certification testing program tracks ten analytes: Pb, tAs, Cd, MeHg, tHg, iAs, Ni, Al, Cr-VI, Sn. The wiki may discuss other metals in the corpus, but product-category threshold-development pages must keep this official analyte list distinct from broader literature metals. See [[docs/schema-history]] for the 8-vs-10 reconciliation.
23:**Frontmatter wikilinks:** Page-reference arrays in frontmatter use the quoted-wikilink form `["[[folder/slug]]", "[[folder/slug]]"]`. Quoting is required because YAML reserves `[` as a flow-sequence delimiter; without quotes, `[[` is parsed as a nested empty list. Wrapping page-reference arrays as wikilinks is what makes Obsidian's graph view surface relationships sourced from frontmatter.
33:All other frontmatter array fields stay bare; they are tag/classifier vocabularies (`metals`, `jurisdictions`, `audience`, `species`, `drivers`, `aliases`, `mechanism`, `disease_links`, `matrices`, `applicable_regulations`, `typical_ingredients`, `near_duplicates`), not page references.
35:Unresolved-target wikilinks (frontmatter or body wikilinks pointing to pages that do not yet exist) are intentional backlog markers, not lint errors. They render as dotted nodes in Obsidian's graph and indicate where the wiki is expected to grow next.
